# Line endings are LF in the repository and LF in the working tree, on every
# platform. Two reasons, and the second one is the one that bites.
#
# api.model.json and include/yo.h are generated and then compared byte for byte
# against the model by `cargo xtask check`. A Windows checkout that rewrites
# every line ending fails that comparison for a reason that has nothing to do
# with the model, and the failure message is unreadable because the difference
# is invisible.
#
# The other reason is that a C header shipped to callers should be the same
# file everywhere. A binding generator that hashes it should get one hash.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Things that are not text and must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.yo binary
